<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SiLS variant of obigo_launch's sample_adsw_control_run.launch.xml, for the Control
  partition. Docs: docs/sils/sils-integration-topology.md §3, sils-stage3-autoware-partition.md

  NOTE ON STYLE: XML comments may not contain a double hyphen, so this file uses "->" and
  plain prose where the rest of the tree would use an em dash. Two hyphens anywhere in here
  is a parse error, not a style nit, and the launch file fails to load with a column number
  that points at the comment rather than the markup.

  ★ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS

  We need autoware_simple_planning_simulator OFF, because in a real rig the plant is MORAI
  or Web.Auto and the SiLS bridges occupy the vehicle_interface seat. The switch is
  `launch_simulator_dummy_vehicle`, declared with a proper default in
  obigo_launch/launch/planning_simulator.launch.xml. But sample_adsw_control_run.launch.xml
  passes it as a `value=`, and a `value=` is not overridable from the command line (only a
  `default=` is), so

      ros2 launch obigo_launch sample_adsw_control_run.launch.xml \
          launch_simulator_dummy_vehicle:=false

  is silently ignored: it sets a variable nothing reads.

  Rather than patch a file inside the vendor image, this include chains one level up, to
  planning_simulator.launch.xml, whose args ARE defaults. Every value below is copied
  verbatim from sample_adsw_control_run.launch.xml except the two marked CHANGED. Keep it
  that way: any drift from the vendor file is a difference in what we are testing.

  ★ THE ARG WE DO NOT TOUCH: vehicle_simulation

  planning_simulator.launch.xml derives Autoware's own vehicle interface from it:

      <let name="launch_vehicle_interface" value="false" if="$(var vehicle_simulation)"/>
      <let name="launch_vehicle_interface" value="true" unless="$(var vehicle_simulation)"/>

  It defaults to true, so launch_vehicle_interface stays FALSE and the seat stays EMPTY,
  which is exactly what we want, because OUR bridges are the vehicle interface. Setting
  vehicle_simulation=false would make Autoware launch its own CAN side interface package
  and fight us for /vehicle/status/*.

  ★ WHAT MUST RUN ALONGSIDE

  Turning the simulator off removes ten publishers, not six. Measured on this partition
  2026-08-11 (docs/sils/evidence/sps-topic-inventory-2026-08-11.txt): 53 subscriptions
  across those ten topics, all with simple_planning_simulator as the sole publisher.

      aw_vehicle_status_bridge   /vehicle/status/*        14 subscriptions
      aw_localization_bridge     /localization/*          38 subscriptions

  Not supplied, and believed harmless here. Verify, do not assume:
      /vehicle/status/actuation_status  MEASURED 0 subscribers. Only
                                        autoware_raw_vehicle_cmd_converter reads it, and
                                        that launches only for a vehicle_model_type
                                        containing ACTUATION_CMD. sample_vehicle is
                                        DELAY_STEER_ACC_GEARED, so it does not run.
      /sensing/imu/imu_data             MEASURED 1 subscriber:
                                        autoware_autonomous_emergency_braking. Whether AEB
                                        blocks control without it is the open question this
                                        configuration exists to answer.

  ★ USAGE

  The file is not in the image. tools/sils/ss2/run_control_partition_sils.sh copies it to
  the /workspace bind mount and restarts only the control container with it. To reproduce
  the vendor behaviour exactly (simulator ON) for an A/B comparison, pass
  launch_simulator_dummy_vehicle:=true, which is what the default below is for.
-->
<launch>
  <arg name="map_path" description="point cloud and lanelet2 map directory path"/>
  <arg name="vehicle_model" default="sample_vehicle"/>
  <arg name="sensor_model" default="sample_sensor_kit"/>
  <arg name="data_path" default="$(env HOME)/autoware_data"/>

  <!-- CHANGED (1 of 2): the whole point of this file. Vendor hardcodes true. -->
  <arg name="launch_simulator_dummy_vehicle" default="false"
       description="launch autoware_simple_planning_simulator. FALSE means the SiLS bridges
                    must supply /vehicle/status/* AND /localization/*; see header."/>

  <include file="$(find-pkg-share obigo_launch)/launch/planning_simulator.launch.xml">
    <arg name="map_path" value="$(var map_path)"/>
    <arg name="vehicle_model" value="$(var vehicle_model)"/>
    <arg name="sensor_model" value="$(var sensor_model)"/>
    <arg name="data_path" value="$(var data_path)"/>
    <arg name="is_launch_autoware" value="true"/>
    <arg name="launch_file" value="adsw_control.launch.xml"/>
    <arg name="is_launch_simulator" value="true"/>
    <arg name="sim_launch_file" value="obigo_simulator_component.launch.xml"/>
    <arg name="launch_simulator_dummy_perception" value="false"/>
    <!-- CHANGED (2 of 2): forwarded from our arg instead of a hardcoded true. -->
    <arg name="launch_simulator_dummy_vehicle" value="$(var launch_simulator_dummy_vehicle)"/>
    <arg name="initial_engage_state" value="true"/>
    <arg name="pointcloud_container_name" value="pointcloud_container_control"/>
    <arg name="glog_name" value="glog_component_control"/>
  </include>
</launch>
